\begin{corollary}
Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{main}, the solution $u$ to problem \eqref{prob} satisfies the following:\begin{enumerate}
\item If $1 < \gamma \leq 1 + 2\mu$, then $u$ is Lipschitz continuous up to the boundary $\partial\Omega$.\
\item If $\gamma > 1 + 2\mu$, then $u \in C^{0, \frac{2}{1 + \gamma - 2\mu}}(\bar\Omega)$.\
\item If $\gamma < 3 - 2\mu$, then $u \in H^1_0(\Omega)$.
\end{enumerate}\end{corollary}

